# libpdx-pds-parser -- caps.decl
#
# Waves:
#   R221 (parser-tier Unicode + lexer umbrella, paideia-os#2485)
#   R222 (cmd-functor umbrella, paideia-os#2486)
#   R223 (pipeline-lang umbrella, paideia-os#2487)
#   R224 (lambda-lang umbrella, paideia-os#2488)
#   R225 (typechecker umbrella, paideia-os#2489)
#   R226 (datalog umbrella, paideia-os#2490)
#   R229 (REPL evaluator umbrella, paideia-os#2493)
# libpdx-pds-parser is a USER-SPACE shared library providing
# parser-tier wrappers over the kernel-side libpdx-unicode-tables
# substrate (R131). Every entry point is a pure leaf (or a leaf that
# delegates to libpdx-unicode-tables) over caller-supplied raw
# pointers.
#
# This file therefore declares the ABSENCE of required capabilities
# at the ENTRY-POINT floor -- a downstream tool linking this library
# does not need to grant anything beyond its own data-buffer read /
# write capability. Every primitive here is `effects: {mem},
# capabilities: {}` or `effects: {}, capabilities: {}` (lib.pdx's
# feature-level accessor is pure).
#
# consumed_kinds: none through all currently-planned M-landings.
#
#   R221.M1 UTF-8 decoder + NFC normalizer: calls into libpdx-
#      unicode-tables's _norm_nfc (R131.M3) via linker-resolved
#      symbol; no KIND surface.
#   R221.M2 grapheme cluster iterator: calls into libpdx-unicode-
#      tables's _gc_next (R131.M2) via linker-resolved symbol; no
#      KIND.
#   R221.M3 width pass: calls into libpdx-unicode-tables's
#      _width_char and _width_str (R131.M5) via linker-resolved
#      symbol; no KIND.
#   R221.M4 context-tracking lexer: pure byte-walker over this
#      library's M1 output buffer; no KIND.
#   R221.M5 unified AST: in-process arena allocator over caller
#      buffer; no KIND.
#   R221.M6 span-mapping NFC variant: emits an additional span-
#      mapping table alongside M1's output; no KIND.
#   R221.M7 fuzz corpus: tests only; no library-time surface.
#   R223.M1 Pipeline stage parser: pure in-process byte-walker +
#      records emitter over the caller's NFC-normalised input and
#      caller-supplied out buffer. Internally CALLs the
#      module-private _pl_emit_word helper. No KIND; no external
#      module dependency.
#   R223.M2 Record projection parser (record_projection.pdx):
#      pure in-process byte-walker + FieldSelector emitter over the
#      caller-supplied argv bytes (the argv of a `select` or
#      `project` pipeline stage, as located inside R223.M1's
#      PipelineStage records). _rp_parse_select / _rp_parse_project
#      are 1-nested-call wrappers that delegate to the module-
#      private _rp_parse_impl (which CALLs the module-private
#      _rp_skip_ws leaf). No KIND; no external module dependency.
#   R223.M3+ pipeline-lang follow-ups: no KIND surface planned;
#      consumers of this library (R222 cmd-functor dispatch,
#      R129.M5 renderer-override post-pass) remain the KIND-
#      touching tier.
#   R222.M1 SchemasSig parser (schemas_sig.pdx): pure in-process
#      byte-walker + field-descriptor emitter over the caller's
#      NFC-normalised input and caller-supplied out buffer.
#      _ss_parse_body CALLs the module-private _sch_sig_skip_ws +
#      _sch_sig_classify_type leaves; _ss_match_record is a M1 stub
#      (returns SS_UNIMPLEMENTED). No KIND; no external module
#      dependency.
#   R222.M2 CommandSig parser (command_sig.pdx): pure in-process
#      byte-walker + header + CapDecl emitter over the caller's
#      NFC-normalised input and caller-supplied out buffer.
#      _cs_parse_body CALLs the module-private _cmd_sig_skip_ws +
#      _cmd_sig_fnv1a64 leaves. No KIND; no external module
#      dependency. The cap-name identity hash is FNV-1a 64 (not
#      BLAKE3), chosen to keep this library pure-leaf; a later
#      R222.M? landing may swap it for a wrapper call to
#      paideia_crypto_blake3_hash without an ABI break (name_hash
#      slot stays u64).
#   R222.M3+ cmd-functor follow-ups: REPL dispatch (M3) consumes
#      the CommandSig record + replaces R222.M1's _ss_match_record
#      stub with a full field-by-field type-code compare. ArgSpec /
#      FlagSpec (M4) and the registry client (M5) layer over the
#      same (header + descriptor array) byte image. Still no KIND
#      surface in this library -- the enclosing shell session is
#      where cap handles reify against the KIND-touching tier.
#   R224.M1 LambdaLit parser: pure in-process byte-walker + header /
#      descriptor emitter over the caller's NFC-normalised input and
#      caller-supplied out buffer. _ll_parse CALLs the module-private
#      _ll_skip_ws / _ll_classify_type / _ll_parse_param helpers. No
#      KIND; no external module dependency.
#   R224.M2 ClosureCapture parser (closure_capture.pdx): pure
#      in-process byte-walker + header + Binding emitter over the
#      caller's NFC-normalised input and caller-supplied out buffer.
#      _cc_parse CALLs the module-private _cc_skip_ws / _cc_parse_binding
#      helpers; _cc_parse_binding in turn CALLs _cc_skip_ws and
#      _cc_classify_type leaves. No KIND; no external module dependency.
#      Parses the OPTIONAL closure-capture list `[binding, binding, ...]`
#      that signals the lambda will cross a process boundary (Q13
#      hybrid serialization). Untyped bindings capture BY_REF (name
#      resolves at receiver); typed bindings `name:type` capture
#      BY_VALUE (sender serializes the value using the declared type).
#   R224.M3+ lambda-lang follow-ups: effect-row inference (M3) reads
#      the LambdaHeader + the CC image Binding modes to seed an effect
#      row; capability-row typing (M4) reads the by-value partition to
#      require serialize-of-type-X caps on the sender; nested-lambda
#      scoping (M5) layers over the same (header + param + capture)
#      byte image. Still no KIND surface in this library -- the
#      enclosing shell session is where effect / cap row ids reify
#      against the KIND-touching tier.
#   R225.M1 HM algorithm W core: pure in-process type-graph walker
#      over a singleton .bss pool (2048-byte TypeNode storage) and
#      the caller-supplied scheme buffers. _hm_fresh_var /
#      _hm_unify / _hm_instantiate / _hm_generalise all touch only
#      the module's own .bss + caller-pointer args. _hm_unify and
#      _hm_occurs are self-recursive via the symbol table; _hm_find
#      is a pure leaf. No KIND; no external module dependency.
#   R225.M2 Row types (row_types.pdx): pure in-process row-graph
#      walker + Remy-style unifier layered over R225.M1's singleton
#      _hm_pool. _rt_find walks the extended resolved chain (TyVar
#      OR ROW_VAR). _rt_alloc_node reserves a 16-byte slot shared
#      with hm_core allocations. _rt_label_hash is a pure-leaf
#      FNV-1a 32 over caller bytes. _rt_row_empty / _rt_row_var /
#      _rt_row_extend are single-nested-CALL allocators. _rt_record_type
#      allocates TyApp(TyCon(RECORD,1), row). _rt_row_select /
#      _rt_row_restrict / _rt_row_concat walk the row chain and
#      allocate new ROW_EXT nodes for restrict/concat results.
#      _rt_row_unify is self-recursive and cross-recursive with
#      _hm_unify (TyVar and TyCon arms delegate; TyApp recurses on
#      children because they may be rows; TyRow uses the Remy pivot
#      on label mismatch). No KIND; no external cross-library
#      dependency (intra-library dep on HmCore for _hm_unify and
#      the _hm_pool / _hm_pool_next / _hm_var_next .bss symbols).
#   R225.M3+ typechecker follow-ups: Datalog predicate types (M3)
#      bridge SchemasSig descriptors (R222.M1) into the pool via a
#      1:1 remap table; effect-row unification (M4) adds a second
#      row kind reusing the TyRow dispatcher via a disjoint subkind
#      code; cross-context flow (M5) chains R225.M2 row shapes
#      through pipeline <-> Datalog boundaries; rank-restricted
#      enforcement (M6) adds a scheme-depth counter. None introduces
#      a KIND surface this library invokes against.
#   R226.M1 Datalog parser: pure in-process byte-walker + Clause-
#      record emitter over the caller's NFC-normalised input and
#      caller-supplied out buffer. _dl_parse CALLs the module-
#      private _dl_skip_ws / _dl_scan_ident_or_var / _dl_scan_number
#      / _dl_scan_string / _dl_scan_body helpers. No KIND; no
#      external module dependency.
#   R226.M2+ datalog follow-ups: predicate-type resolution (M2)
#      calls into R220.M4 schema registry via linker-resolved
#      symbol; evaluator (M3+) runs over R127.M7 history_facts via
#      the direct-call API _hf_query_by_* (which the shell owns, not
#      this library). This library stays leaf.
#   R229.M2 SessionEnv (session_env.pdx): pure in-process persistent
#      binding store over a singleton .bss pool (8 KiB env pool + 64 B
#      head-table). _se_init / _se_init_session are pure leaves that
#      touch only this module's own .bss. _se_insert_binding /
#      _se_lookup_binding / _se_unset_binding are pure-leaf scanners
#      over the per-session row with 6-push callee-save frames and no
#      nested CALLs. The type-pool interpretation of the stored
#      type_ref u32 is HmCore's responsibility (SessionEnv does NOT
#      call into HmCore -- the shell-side REPL dispatch, at R229.M3+,
#      does, and merely hands the pool_idx through). No KIND; no
#      external module dependency; no cross-library dependency.
#   R229.M3+ REPL evaluator follow-ups: dispatch (M3) parses `let`/
#      `unset` from the R229.M1 line_buf, calls HM typecheck +
#      evaluator and routes into this module. Teardown cascade
#      wire-up (M4) folds `_se_init_session` into
#      `_shell_session_destroy`. Exported bindings (M4) use the
#      SessionEnv flags byte. Lexical nested scopes (M5) add a stack
#      of SessionEnv rows per session. Persistent per-user env (M6)
#      layers a pdxfs serialisation hook. None introduces a KIND
#      surface this library invokes against.
#
# None of the planned landings is expected to introduce a KIND
# surface this library itself invokes against. The parser is a
# passive linker artifact.
#
# declares_output_schemas: none. The parser emits no semantic-pipe
# records; its only user-visible outputs are the packed-u64 return
# values documented at each entry point in src/*.pdx. A downstream
# consumer (e.g. the shell's lexer at R221.M4+, the LSP bridge at
# R221.M6) that chooses to log a parse fingerprint does so via its
# own `klog_s1_*` wrapper on its own schema -- this library's
# primitives neither call klog nor know about one.
#
# ---- Error band 0x2700..0x27FF (R221.M1, utf8_nfc) -------------------
#
# Small-value user-space packed-status range. Four slots used at M1:
#
#   U8N_OK                 : 0        normalise succeeded.
#   U8N_ERR_INVALID_UTF8   : 0x2700   input not RFC 3629 well-formed.
#   U8N_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL  : 0x2701   out_cap < NFC output byte count.
#   U8N_ERR_NORMALIZE_FAIL : 0x2702   reserved for post-M1 normaliser-
#                                     internal failure (never returned
#                                     at M1).
#
# The 0x2700..0x27FF range is reserved for parser-tier packed-status
# codes across R221. The remaining 0x2703..0x27FF slots are reserved
# for M2+ error kinds (e.g. GRAPHEME_INVALID_UTF8 at M2, LEX_UNEXPECTED
# _TOKEN at M4, AST_ARENA_FULL at M5).
#
# ---- Error band 0x2B00..0x2BFF (R223.M1, pipeline) -------------------
#
# Pipeline-tier packed-status range. Five slots used at R223.M1:
#
#   PL_OK                     : 0        parse succeeded.
#   PL_ERR_TOO_MANY_STAGES    : 0x2B00   > PL_MAX_STAGES (16).
#   PL_ERR_TOO_MANY_ARGS      : 0x2B01   > PL_MAX_ARGS (8) per stage.
#   PL_ERR_UNTERMINATED_QUOTE : 0x2B02   DQ or SQ open at EOI.
#   PL_ERR_EMPTY_STAGE        : 0x2B03   `||`, leading or trailing `|`.
#   PL_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL      : 0x2B04   out_cap < needed stage count * 64.
#
# The 0x2B00..0x2BFF range is reserved for pipeline-lang parser
# packed-status codes across R223. Slots 0x2B05..0x2BFF reserved for
# R223.M2+ (redir ops, @hostname annotations, etc.).
#
# Not to be confused with the kernel-side Pipeline module's
# PL_ERR_BAD_ARGS / PL_ERR_TOO_MANY / PL_ERR_DST_OVERFLOW codes which
# occupy a wholly separate 0xFFFFEC40..42 band and name a different
# (planner-side) module.
#
# ---- Error band 0x2C00..0x2CFF (R224.M1, lambda_lit) ----------------
#
# Lambda-lang parser-tier packed-status range. Five slots used at
# R224.M1:
#
#   LL_OK                  : 0        parse succeeded.
#   LL_ERR_SYNTAX          : 0x2C00   grammar mismatch at ident,
#                                     ':', '(', ')', or ','.
#   LL_ERR_TOO_MANY_PARAMS : 0x2C01   > LL_MAX_PARAMS (8).
#   LL_ERR_UNKNOWN_TYPE    : 0x2C02   type_name not in the M1 set
#                                     ({u64,i64,str,hex,hash32,tsc,
#                                       path,pid}).
#   LL_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL   : 0x2C03   out_cap < 32 + n_params*32 +
#                                     body_len.
#   LL_ERR_NO_ARROW        : 0x2C04   ParamList terminator was not
#                                     `->` (dedicated code so the
#                                     diagnostic can point at the
#                                     missing-arrow site rather than
#                                     at a generic SYNTAX).
#
# The 0x2C00..0x2CFF range is reserved for lambda-lang parser packed-
# status codes across R224. Slots 0x2C05..0x2CFF reserved for R224.M2+
# (expression parse, effect-row inference, capability-row typing,
# nested-lambda scoping, destructuring-pattern mismatch, etc.).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3600..0x36FF (R225.M2, row_types) ------------------
#
# Typechecker-tier packed-status range for the SECOND R225 wave --
# ROW TYPES: Remy-style row polymorphism for records with named
# fields, layered over R225.M1's TypeNode pool. Seven slots used at
# R225.M2:
#
#   RT_OK                 : 0        row op succeeded.
#   RT_ERR_LABEL_MISSING  : 0x3600   _rt_row_select/_rt_row_restrict
#                                    label not found in row.
#   RT_ERR_LABEL_DUP      : 0x3601   _rt_row_concat label collision.
#   RT_ERR_POOL_FULL      : 0x3602   HmCore pool exhausted (shared
#                                    with hm_core; row allocations
#                                    draw from the same singleton
#                                    _hm_pool).
#   RT_ERR_KIND_MISMATCH  : 0x3603   _rt_row_unify saw a row-vs-non-row
#                                    pair where kinds disagree.
#   RT_ERR_CLOSED_ROW     : 0x3604   _rt_row_unify saw EMPTY vs EXT;
#                                    _rt_row_concat refused an open
#                                    (ROW_VAR-tailed) first operand.
#   RT_ERR_OCCURS         : 0x3605   reserved for M4+ row-var cycle
#                                    detection (M2 relies on hm_core's
#                                    TyVar occurs-check for shared
#                                    type-level cycles; the row-var
#                                    chain depth is bounded by pool
#                                    size, so a dedicated row-occurs
#                                    check is a conservative no-op at
#                                    M2 and the slot is reserved).
#   RT_ERR_MISMATCH       : 0x3606   field-type unification failure
#                                    bubbled up from a nested
#                                    _rt_row_unify or _hm_unify call;
#                                    equivalent at the top-level
#                                    protocol surface to hm_core's
#                                    HM_ERR_MISMATCH (0x2D01) but
#                                    carried in the row-tier band so
#                                    the caller's error path can
#                                    discriminate "row operation
#                                    failed" from "pure HM operation
#                                    failed".
#
# The 0x3600..0x36FF range is reserved for R225.M2+ row types. Slots
# 0x3607..0x36FF reserved for R225.M3 (predicate-type bridge),
# R225.M4 (effect rows -- disjoint subkind), R225.M5 (cross-context
# flow), R225.M6 (rank-2 refusal), and R225.M7 (error-span wrapping).
#
# R225.M1 (hm_core) owns the disjoint 0x2D00..0x2DFF band; the two
# R225 submodules do not share status codes because a downstream
# dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "pure HM
# operation failed" from "row operation failed". The parallel
# R224.M2 band (0x3500..0x35FF) and R229.M2 band (0x3700..0x37FF)
# sit outside this range; the three parallel M2 arms of Wave 117
# chose non-adjacent slices to simplify the disjointness proof.
#
# ---- Error band 0x2D00..0x2DFF (R225.M1, hm_core) --------------------
#
# Typechecker-tier packed-status range. Four slots used at R225.M1:
#
#   HM_OK                 : 0        unification / instantiation /
#                                    generalisation succeeded.
#   HM_ERR_OCCURS         : 0x2D00   cyclic unification caught by the
#                                    occurs-check (TyVar binds to a
#                                    type that mentions itself).
#   HM_ERR_MISMATCH       : 0x2D01   constructor or arity mismatch;
#                                    also returned on malformed scheme
#                                    (bad body-relative index, unknown
#                                    kind code, env ref out-of-range).
#   HM_ERR_POOL_FULL      : 0x2D02   128-node TypeNode pool exhausted.
#   HM_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL  : 0x2D03   out_cap < scheme-size required by
#                                    _hm_generalise, or scheme_len
#                                    inconsistent with its header at
#                                    _hm_instantiate.
#
# The 0x2D00..0x2DFF range is reserved for R225 typechecker packed-
# status codes. Slots 0x2D04..0x2DFF reserved for R225.M2+ (row-type
# mismatches, effect-row saturation, rank-2 refusal, missing predicate
# schema, etc.).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3500..0x35FF (R224.M2, closure_capture) ------------
#
# Lambda closure-capture parser-tier packed-status range. Six slots
# used at R224.M2:
#
#   CC_OK                    : 0        parse succeeded.
#   CC_ERR_SYNTAX            : 0x3500   grammar mismatch at ident, ':',
#                                       ',', or peek after ident.
#   CC_ERR_TOO_MANY_BINDINGS : 0x3501   > CC_MAX_BINDINGS (16).
#   CC_ERR_UNKNOWN_TYPE      : 0x3502   type_name not in the M2 set
#                                       ({u64,i64,str,hex,hash32,tsc,
#                                         path,pid}).
#   CC_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL     : 0x3503   out_cap < 32 + n_bindings*32.
#   CC_ERR_NO_OPEN           : 0x3504   first non-whitespace byte was
#                                       not `[`.
#   CC_ERR_NO_CLOSE          : 0x3505   EOI before matching `]`.
#
# The 0x3500..0x35FF range is reserved for the R224.M2 closure-capture
# parser band. R224.M1 (LambdaLit) owns a disjoint 0x2C00..0x2CFF band
# -- the two R224 submodules do not share status codes because a
# downstream dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "the
# lambda header faulted" from "the explicit capture list faulted".
# Slots 0x3506..0x35FF reserved for R224.M3+ (per-binding effect-row
# mismatch, capability-row mismatch, let-rec recursive capture failure,
# linear/affine propagation violation, etc.).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3700..0x37FF (R229.M2, session_env) ----------------
#
# Session-env packed-status range for the R229 REPL-evaluator wave.
# Five slots used at R229.M2:
#
#   SE_OK                   : 0        operation succeeded.
#   SE_ERR_BAD_SESSION      : 0x3700   session_id >= SE_MAX_SESSIONS (8).
#   SE_ERR_BAD_NAME         : 0x3701   name_len == 0 or > SE_NAME_MAX (16).
#   SE_ERR_TOO_MANY         : 0x3702   head == SE_MAX_BINDINGS (32) on
#                                      insert of a new (not-yet-present)
#                                      name.
#   SE_ERR_NOT_FOUND        : 0x3703   lookup or unset against a name
#                                      not present in the session env
#                                      (or present only as a tombstone).
#   SE_ERR_BAD_SCHEME_KIND  : 0x3704   insert called with scheme_kind
#                                      not in {SE_SCHEME_DIRECT (1),
#                                      SE_SCHEME_BLOB (2)}.
#
# The 0x3700..0x37FF range is reserved for the R229 session-env band.
# R229.M1 (kernel-side REPL loop) owns a disjoint 0x3000..0x30FF band
# (RL_ERR_*) -- the two R229 submodules do not share status codes
# because a downstream dispatcher's compound error path must
# distinguish "the per-cycle state machine faulted" from "the
# session-scoped binding store faulted". Slots 0x3705..0x37FF reserved
# for R229.M3+ (SE_ERR_HM_POOL_FULL when SessionEnv proxies the HM
# layer's pool-full, SE_ERR_TOMBSTONE_EXHAUSTED on compaction failure,
# SE_ERR_EXPORTED_IMMUTABLE on cross-session rebind of an exported
# binding, etc.).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3800..0x38FF (R221.M2, grapheme_iter) --------------
#
# TR#29 grapheme-cluster-boundary iterator packed-status range.
#
#   GI_STATUS_OK           : 0        advance/retreat succeeded.
#   GI_STATUS_EOF          : 1        _gi_next_cluster: cursor_byte at EOI.
#   GI_STATUS_BOF          : 1        _gi_prev_cluster: cursor_byte at 0.
#   GI_ERR_INVALID_UTF8    : 0x3800   substrate (libpdx-unicode-tables
#                                     R131.M2 _gc_next) returned the
#                                     INVALID_UTF8 status; propagated
#                                     through with cursor_byte preserved.
#   GI_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL   : 0x3801   _gi_tokenize_args: out_cap < the
#                                     emitted descriptor stride.
#   GI_ERR_TOO_MANY_TOKENS : 0x3802   _gi_tokenize_args: emitted token
#                                     count > GI_MAX_TOKENS.
#   GI_ERR_BAD_CURSOR      : 0x3803   _gi_prev_cluster: cursor_byte >
#                                     bytes_len.
#
# The 0x3800..0x38FF range is reserved for grapheme-iterator packed-
# status codes across R221.M2+. R221.M1 (UTF-8 + NFC decoder) owns a
# disjoint parser-tier band -- the two R221 submodules do not share
# status codes because a downstream dispatcher must distinguish
# "the decoder faulted" from "the cluster iterator faulted". Slots
# 0x3804..0x38FF reserved for R221.M3+ follow-ups (width-pass
# TR#11 integration, line-break TR#14 integration).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3900..0x39FF (R222.M3, functor_instance) ----------
#
# Functor-instantiation materialization-record packed-status range.
#
#   FI_OK                 : 0        parse + elaboration succeeded.
#   FI_ERR_SYNTAX         : 0x3900   bad grammar at current cursor.
#   FI_ERR_NAME_MISMATCH  : 0x3901   parsed name does not match a
#                                    functor in the CommandSig body
#                                    (R222.M2) catalogue.
#   FI_ERR_TOO_MANY_ARGS  : 0x3902   arg_count > FI_MAX_ARGS (16).
#   FI_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL  : 0x3903   out_cap < 64 + arg_count*32.
#   FI_ERR_BAD_CS_RECORD  : 0x3904   command-sig record magic mismatch
#                                    (cs_len < 128 or cs magic != CSIG;
#                                    also materialization record magic
#                                    mismatch not FINS).
#   FI_ERR_ELABORATION    : 0x3905   per-arg elaboration failed.
#   FI_ERR_UNKNOWN_TYPE   : 0x3906   per-arg type_code not in the
#                                    expected set for the functor's
#                                    typed signature.
#
# The 0x3900..0x39FF range is reserved for functor-instantiation
# packed-status codes across R222.M3+. R222.M1/M2 (SchemasSig,
# CommandSig) own disjoint 0x3200/0x3300 bands -- the three R222
# submodules do not share status codes because a downstream
# dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "schemas-sig
# faulted" vs "command-sig faulted" vs "functor-instantiation
# faulted". Slots 0x3907..0x39FF reserved for R222.M4+ follow-ups
# (ArgSpec typing failures, FlagSpec typing failures, registry
# miss, commands.toml bind failure, describe-rendering failure,
# per-turn fuzz-corpus deviations).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3400..0x34FF (R223.M2, record_projection) ----------
#
# Pipeline-tier packed-status range for the SECOND R223 wave --
# RECORD PROJECTION, the `select FIELDS` / `project FIELDS` pipeline
# operators that filter the typed-record stream by field name. Three
# slots used at R223.M2:
#
#   RP_OK                  : 0        parse succeeded.
#   RP_ERR_SYNTAX          : 0x3400   grammar mismatch (bad first byte,
#                                     empty field, > 14-byte name,
#                                     missing or trailing comma, EOI
#                                     before any field).
#   RP_ERR_TOO_MANY_FIELDS : 0x3401   > RP_MAX_FIELDS (32).
#   RP_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL   : 0x3402   out_cap < n_fields * 16.
#
# The 0x3400..0x34FF range is reserved for record-projection packed-
# status codes across R223.M2+. R223.M1 (pipeline stage parser) owns
# a disjoint 0x2B00..0x2BFF band -- the two R223 modules do not share
# status codes because a downstream dispatcher's compound error path
# must distinguish "the outer pipeline tokeniser faulted" from "the
# inner RecordProjection argv parser faulted". Slots 0x3403..0x34FF
# reserved for R223.M3+ (differentiation between `select` reorder
# semantics and `project` drop-unselected semantics; wildcards; name
# aliases).
#
# The 0x2F00..0x32FF gap between the R226 band (0x2EFF) and the new
# R222.M2 CommandSig band (0x3300..0x33FF, documented below) is
# reserved for R227+ parser-tier primitives (pds container header
# parse, pipeline-record row types, Datalog predicate-type bridge,
# etc.) that will land before R223.M3's semantic split.
#
# ---- Error band 0x3300..0x33FF (R222.M2, command_sig) ----------------
#
# Cmd-functor-identity parser packed-status range. Four slots used at
# R222.M2:
#
#   CS_OK                     : 0        parse succeeded.
#   CS_ERR_SYNTAX             : 0x3300   grammar mismatch at keyword,
#                                        ':', '"', hex rights, or ident
#                                        byte-class.
#   CS_ERR_TOO_MANY_CAPS      : 0x3301   > CS_MAX_CAPS (8).
#   CS_ERR_UNKNOWN_STABILITY  : 0x3302   stability value not in the
#                                        {stable, experimental,
#                                         deprecated} set.
#   CS_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL      : 0x3303   out_cap < CS_HEADER_BYTES (128)
#                                        + n_caps * CS_CAP_DESC_BYTES
#                                        (32).
#
# The 0x3300..0x33FF range is reserved for the R222 cmd-functor-identity
# parser band. R222.M1 (SchemasSig) owns a disjoint 0x2A00..0x2AFF
# band -- the two R222 submodules do not share status codes because a
# downstream dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "the
# input/output record shape faulted" from "the functor identity
# declaration faulted". Slots 0x3304..0x33FF reserved for R222.M3+
# (REPL dispatch typecheck mismatch, ArgSpec/FlagSpec parse errors,
# registry client lookup miss, etc.).
#
# Not to be confused with the kernel-side Pipeline module's
# PL_ERR_BAD_ARGS / PL_ERR_TOO_MANY / PL_ERR_DST_OVERFLOW codes which
# occupy a wholly separate 0xFFFFEC40..42 band and name a different
# (planner-side) module.
#
# ---- Error band 0x2E00..0x2EFF (R226.M1, datalog) --------------------
#
# Datalog-tier packed-status range. Five slots used at R226.M1:
#
#   DL_OK                      : 0        parse succeeded.
#   DL_ERR_SYNTAX              : 0x2E00   grammar mismatch.
#   DL_ERR_TOO_MANY_CLAUSES    : 0x2E01   > DL_MAX_CLAUSES (256).
#   DL_ERR_TOO_MANY_TERMS      : 0x2E02   > DL_MAX_TERMS (4) per head.
#   DL_ERR_UNTERMINATED_STRING : 0x2E03   `"..."` open at EOI.
#   DL_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL       : 0x2E04   out_cap < needed clause count * 48.
#
# The 0x2E00..0x2EFF range is reserved for datalog parser packed-
# status codes across R226 (slots 0x2E05..0x2EFF reserved for M2+
# predicate-type resolution, semi-naive evaluator, aggregation,
# stratified negation, session-local EDB, etc.).
#
# The 0x2C00..0x2CFF range (previously documented as "R225.M*
# reserved" in pipeline.pdx's namespace map) is now the live R224
# lambda-lang band. R225.M1 consumes the 0x2D00..0x2DFF slice of the
# former shared reservation; R226 carves out 0x2E00..0x2EFF cleanly
# above that. R223.M2 (RecordProjection) carves 0x3400..0x34FF
# ABOVE the contiguous R221..R226 block rather than reusing the
# adjacent 0x2B05..0x2BFF slot of R223.M1's pipeline band -- the
# two R223 submodules remain error-disjoint so a downstream
# dispatcher's compound error path can distinguish outer-pipeline
# faults from inner-projection faults. The pipeline.pdx comment-
# level reservation note is superseded by this caps.decl entry.
#
# R224.M2 (ClosureCapture) carves 0x3500..0x35FF; R225.M2 (RowTypes)
# carves 0x3600..0x36FF; R229.M2 (SessionEnv) carves 0x3700..0x37FF.
# The three M2 bands of Wave 117 sit on non-adjacent kilo-step
# boundaries so a downstream dispatcher's compound error path can
# discriminate at a glance which satellite submodule faulted, and
# the slices are large enough to accommodate the full M-wave
# decomposition each submodule declares.
#
# R221.M2 (GraphemeIter) carves 0x3800..0x38FF; R222.M3 (FunctorInstance)
# carves 0x3900..0x39FF. Both land in Wave 118 on non-adjacent kilo-step
# boundaries disjoint from every prior wave's bands.
#
# ---- Disjointness proof (all bands) ----------------------------------
#
# All codes fit in a 32-bit unsigned, placed in the low 32 bits of
# packed returns. Disjoint from every other user-space packed-status
# range in the paideia-os tree:
#
#   * libpdx-unicode-tables UTF-8 band: 0xFFFFE700..0xFFFFE70F (large;
#                                       returned raw, not packed)
#   * libpdx-unicode-tables M2..M7 bands: 0xFFFFE710..0xFFFFE77F (large)
#   * libpdx-elevate: 0xFFFFE5E0..EF, 0xFFFFEA00..7F (large)
#   * libpdx-volume internal 0x0100-band (lpv_errors.pdx)
#   * paideia-os shell: 0xFFFFECD/ECE/ED8..EDF (large)
#   * paideia-os mv: 0xFFFFEBC/EBD (large)
#   * paideia-os kernel Pipeline: 0xFFFFEC40..0xFFFFEC42 (large)
#   * kernel drivers: 0xFFFFFC_/FFFFFD_ clusters (large, disjoint)
#
# Grep confirmation at landing time:
#
#   grep -rE '0x2(7)0[0-9A-F]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file + src/utf8_nfc.pdx.
#   grep -rE '0x2B0[0-4]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file + src/pipeline.pdx
#        + design/shell/pipeline-stage-parser.md.
#   grep -rE '0x2C0[0-4]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file + src/lambda_lit.pdx
#        + design/shell/lambda-literal-grammar.md.
#   grep -rE '0x2D0[0-3]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file + src/hm_core.pdx
#        + design/shell/hm-algorithm-w-core.md.
#   grep -rE '0x2E0[0-4]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file + src/datalog.pdx
#        + design/shell/datalog-parser.md.
#   grep -rE '0x340[0-2]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file +
#        src/record_projection.pdx +
#        design/shell/pipeline-record-projection.md. (0x3400 as a
#        Unicode code point in libpdx-unicode-tables/src/width.pdx,
#        as a boot-witness stage marker in tests/kernel/drivers/hda
#        /bdl_synth.pdx and tests/kernel/cap/owner_sweep_synth.pdx,
#        and 0x34000 as a cap manifest flag in src/kernel/boot/
#        witness/r29_registry.pdx are NOT packed-status codes and
#        sit in disjoint semantic namespaces.)
#   grep -rE '0x330[0-3]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file + src/command_sig.pdx
#        + design/shell/cmd-functor-command-sig.md.
#   grep -rE '0x350[0-5]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file +
#        src/closure_capture.pdx + design/shell/closure-capture.md.
#   grep -rE '0x360[0-6]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file + src/row_types.pdx
#        + design/shell/row-types-remy.md.
#   grep -rE '0x370[0-4]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file + src/session_env.pdx
#        + design/shell/session-env.md.
#   grep -rE '0x380[0-3]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file + src/grapheme_iter.pdx
#        + design/shell/grapheme-cluster-boundaries-tr29.md.
#   grep -rE '0x390[0-6]' paideia-os/{src,tools,design,tests}
#     -> no packed-status hits outside this file +
#        src/functor_instance.pdx +
#        design/shell/functor-instantiation.md.
#
# ---- Linker dependencies ---------------------------------------------
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R221.M1 (utf8_nfc.pdx) references these external
# symbols that must be resolved at link time:
#
#   _norm_nfc  (from libpdx-unicode-tables::Normalize, R131.M3,
#               tools/user/libpdx-unicode-tables/build-out/)
#
# A consumer linking this library passes
# `--extra-obj-dir tools/user/libpdx-unicode-tables/build-out` to
# `paideia-as link` so the symbol resolves. If the consumer wants
# only `_u8n_quick_check_ascii` (which has no nested call), it can
# link this library standalone -- the unresolved `_norm_nfc` reference
# is only reached from `_u8n_decode_and_normalize`.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R223.M1 (pipeline.pdx) has NO external linker
# dependencies -- `_pl_parse` only calls `_pl_emit_word` which lives
# in the same object. Both entry points can be linked standalone.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R223.M2 (record_projection.pdx) has NO external
# linker dependencies -- `_rp_parse_select` and `_rp_parse_project`
# are 1-nested-call wrappers that CALL the module-private
# `_rp_parse_impl`, which in turn CALLs the module-private
# `_rp_skip_ws` leaf; all three (plus the two wrappers) live in the
# same object. All four public entry points (`_rp_skip_ws`,
# `_rp_parse_impl`, `_rp_parse_select`, `_rp_parse_project`) can be
# linked standalone.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R224.M1 (lambda_lit.pdx) has NO external linker
# dependencies -- `_ll_parse` only calls the three module-private
# helpers (`_ll_skip_ws`, `_ll_classify_type`, `_ll_parse_param`)
# which all live in the same object; `_ll_parse_param` in turn calls
# the same two leaf helpers. All four public entry points can be
# linked standalone. R224.M2+ (expression parse) will introduce an
# intra-library dependency on R221.M5 AST once that lands; no
# cross-library dependency is planned.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R224.M2 (closure_capture.pdx) has NO external
# linker dependencies -- `_cc_parse` only calls the module-private
# helpers (`_cc_skip_ws`, `_cc_parse_binding`); `_cc_parse_binding`
# in turn calls `_cc_skip_ws` and `_cc_classify_type`. All four
# public entry points can be linked standalone. The R224.M2.5
# integration pass (filed as an umbrella follow-up) will add a
# one-way intra-library dependency where lambda_lit.pdx's `_ll_parse`
# CALLs this module's `_cc_parse`; no cross-library dependency is
# planned at that milestone either.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R225.M1 (hm_core.pdx) has NO external linker
# dependencies -- `_hm_fresh_var`, `_hm_unify`, `_hm_instantiate`,
# `_hm_generalise` only reference the module-private `_hm_find` and
# `_hm_occurs` helpers plus their own self-recursive calls
# (`_hm_unify` and `_hm_occurs` recurse via the symbol table). All
# four public entry points can be linked standalone.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R225.M2 (row_types.pdx) has NO external
# cross-library linker dependencies. It introduces an INTRA-library
# dependency on R225.M1 (hm_core.pdx) at two symbols:
#
#   _hm_unify   -- called by _rt_row_unify's TyVar and TyCon arms
#                  (the pure HM subset of the type grammar is
#                  canonically handled by hm_core's unifier).
#   _hm_pool / _hm_pool_next / _hm_var_next  -- the shared .bss
#                  singleton that _rt_find / _rt_alloc_node /
#                  _rt_row_var reference via `lea r11, [rip+sym]`
#                  (same cross-module .bss precedent as
#                  audit_record.pdx and mkfs.pdxfs/refusal.pdx).
#
# Within the module, _rt_row_unify, _rt_row_select, _rt_row_restrict,
# _rt_row_concat and the row allocators form a self-contained
# recursive clique. _rt_row_unify is also cross-recursive with
# _hm_unify (and _hm_unify's own self-recursion still terminates
# because any _hm_unify call made from _rt_row_unify is over types
# that are either TyVar or TyCon or pure TyApp subterms -- a pure
# TyApp subterm will never reach back into the row branch because
# _rt_row_unify's TyApp arm handles that case directly without
# delegating to _hm_unify).
#
# R225.M3+ (Datalog predicate types, effect rows) will introduce
# cross-module linker deps against R222 (SchemasSig bridge) and
# R220.M4 (schema registry) once those pre-reqs close.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R226.M1 (datalog.pdx) has NO external linker
# dependencies -- `_dl_parse` only calls the five module-private
# helpers (`_dl_skip_ws`, `_dl_scan_ident_or_var`, `_dl_scan_number`,
# `_dl_scan_string`, `_dl_scan_body`) which all live in the same
# object. R226.M2+ (predicate-type resolution against the schema
# registry) will introduce a cross-module linker dep once R220.M4
# lands.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R222.M1 (schemas_sig.pdx) has NO external linker
# dependencies -- `_ss_parse_body` only calls the two module-private
# helpers (`_sch_sig_skip_ws`, `_sch_sig_classify_type`) which both
# live in the same object; `_ss_match_record` is a leaf M1 stub. All
# three public entry points can be linked standalone.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R222.M2 (command_sig.pdx) has NO external linker
# dependencies -- `_cs_parse_body` only calls the two module-private
# helpers (`_cmd_sig_skip_ws`, `_cmd_sig_fnv1a64`) which both live in
# the same object. All three public entry points can be linked
# standalone. R222.M3+ (REPL dispatch, _ss_match_record real body)
# may introduce intra-library deps against the R222.M1 SchemasSig
# arrays and R225.M1 HmCore type-graph pool once the REPL layer wires
# them up; no cross-library dependency is planned.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R229.M2 (session_env.pdx) has NO external linker
# dependencies -- `_se_init`, `_se_init_session`,
# `_se_insert_binding`, `_se_lookup_binding`, `_se_unset_binding` all
# touch only this module's own .bss (`_se_env_pool`,
# `_se_head_table`) and caller-supplied pointer args. There is NO
# cross-module call: SessionEnv STORES a HmCore pool-index as the
# type_ref payload but does not DEREFERENCE it; the REPL dispatch at
# R229.M3+ reads the pool_idx out and calls HmCore directly. All
# five public entry points can be linked standalone. R229.M3+ (REPL
# dispatch) will introduce intra-library deps against this module
# (the REPL layer wires _se_lookup_binding into HM typecheck free-
# name resolution and _se_insert_binding into the EVAL stage); no
# cross-library dependency is planned.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R221.M2 (grapheme_iter.pdx) depends on
# libpdx-unicode-tables at a single external symbol:
#
#   _gc_next  (from libpdx-unicode-tables::GraphemeClusters, R131.M2,
#              tools/user/libpdx-unicode-tables/build-out/)
#
# The ASCII fast path never calls out (pure leaf); the slow path and
# `_gi_tokenize_args` route through `_gc_next` to walk the TR#29
# state machine over the Latin+emoji baseline. Consumers that need
# only ASCII handling can link this library standalone.
#
# libpdx-pds-parser.R222.M3 (functor_instance.pdx) has NO external
# linker dependencies -- `_fi_instantiate` and
# `_fi_elaborate_args` call only module-private helpers
# (`_fi_skip_ws`, `_fi_fnv1a64`, `_fi_lookup_cs`); the CommandSig
# body is passed in by the caller as a flat byte buffer rather
# than via a cross-module call. All public entry points can be
# linked standalone. R222.M4+ may introduce intra-library deps on
# R222.M1 SchemasSig arrays once ArgSpec/FlagSpec lands.
